## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design end-to-end CAPA for a secrets rotation bug with tenant isolation across regions, including data capture, lifecycle, APIs, metrics, and rollout controls.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model capturing tenant context, vault/version, exposure window, evidence, remediation.
- Region-aware lifecycle with states: detected, contained, eradicated, verified, closed.
- Minimal REST API: create/update CAPA, link logs/traces, idempotent operations.
- Metrics: recurrence rate, MTTR per region, false-positive rate, time-to-containment.
- RCA template and canary rollout validation plan before global deployment.

## Code Example

```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  incidentId: string;
  tenantId: string;
  vaultVersion: string;
  exposureWindowMs: number;
  evidenceLinks: string[];
  remediation: string;
  state: "detected" | "contained" | "eradicated" | "verified" | "closed";
  region: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the rotation gate cannot be bypassed in CI/CD pipelines?
- Which metrics best differentiate false positives from real exposures, and how would you alert on them?
- What logging/tracing strategy ties CAPAs to specific secrets and Vault rotations across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CAPA from data governance, not just incident response.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model for evidence, artifacts, and policy checks
- Lifecycle state machine with DETECT → INVESTIGATE → CONTAIN → REMEDIATE → VERIFY → CLOSED
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA creation/update with linked traces
- Region-aware compliance metrics (violation rate, MTTR, FP rate)
- RCA template and canary rollout with automated data redaction

## Code Example
```javascript
// CAPA data model sketch (TypeScript)
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  policyChecks: string[];
  region: string;
  state: 'DETECTED'|'INVESTIGATING'|'CONTAINED'|'REMEDIATED'|'VERIFIED'|'CLOSED';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you surface policy checks in runtime dashboards?
- How would you automate data redaction in canary tests before broader rollout?
